<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan, Belgian firms plan phosphates plant.</title>
<headline>Moroccan, Belgian firms plan phosphates plant.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's phosphates firm, Office Cherifien des Phosphates (OCP), and Belgiam firm Prayon-Rupel are to set up a joint company to build a chemical plant in Morocco, OCP said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that agreement had been reached to build a sodium tripolyphosphate plant at Jorf Lasfar, with an initial capacity of 50,000 tonnes per year.</p>
<p>This could be expanded to 100,000 tonnes annually.</p>
<p>No costs or further details were immediately available.</p>
</text>
